msgid "Extract translatable strings (POT)"
msgstr ""

#: processes/global-tasks.bpmn:47
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Findings: EDIT the one open issue carrying the tracking label (the `label` input) if there is one, otherwise create it, with the report as the body. One issue edited in place, never a new issue or a comment per run, so the tracking issue never becomes a feed."
msgstr ""

#: processes/global-tasks.bpmn:116
#. Diagram label
msgid "Inject the PO into translated Markdown"
msgstr ""

#: processes/global-tasks.bpmn:46
#. Diagram label
msgid "Open or EDIT the one tracking issue"
msgstr ""

#: processes/global-tasks.bpmn:117
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Read the .po file and the source .md, substitute msgstr for msgid, unshield the placeholders, and write the translated .md to translations/<locale>/. Check structure (paragraph count, heading levels) and completeness (no empty msgstr), and lint (doubled punctuation, orphaned placeholders). Tool: the translation_inject MCP tool."
msgstr ""

#: processes/global-tasks.bpmn:70
#. Diagram label
msgid "Record the sign-off as a requirement-signoff attestation"
msgstr ""

#: processes/global-tasks.bpmn:129
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Record the translation's standing in translations/<locale>/status.json. The `official` input says which: `false` records it as unofficial ({ official: false, generatedBy, generatedAt }), usable but shown with a warning badge; `true` records the human sign-off with the SHA-256 of the source .md, so a later change to the source marks it stale."
msgstr ""

#: processes/global-tasks.bpmn:103
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Records that a removal was considered and refused, or that a preview still stands because a signal fired; without the entry that leaves no trace, and nobody can tell why a preview is still up. A reason is REQUIRED — the tool refuses without one."
msgstr ""

#: processes/global-tasks.bpmn:95
#. Diagram label
msgid "Report what would move — sizes, and what breaks"
msgstr ""

#: processes/global-tasks.bpmn:122
#. Diagram label
msgid "Round-trip translation QA"
msgstr ""

#: processes/global-tasks.bpmn:111
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Scan the source content and write the translatable strings to .pot files at the configured granularity: segment prose by paragraph, shield what must not be translated (math, code, labels, Lean companions) as placeholders, normalise whitespace, and extract metadata such as titles, alt text and captions. Tool: the translation_extract MCP tool."
msgstr ""

#: processes/global-tasks.bpmn:31
#. Diagram label
msgid "Session record"
msgstr ""

#: processes/global-tasks.bpmn:96
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The agent reports and waits: what would move, how large, what in the parent breaks, and the rollback. `deletion-requires-confirmation` is not a courtesy to waive: an agent never removes or relocates a durable artefact on its own initiative."
msgstr ""

#: processes/global-tasks.bpmn:71
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "THE RECORD, and not relaxable, because a judgement nobody wrote down is indistinguishable from one never made (`adjudication`, A_RecordEntry). Append one `requirement-signoff` record to `test/attestations/requirement-signoff/<set slug>.attestations.json` — who (kind, id, actor), at, scope (the set or one member), the outcome from the requirement-set code list, the stage it moves the set to, the reason, and the permalink to the issue comment where it was decided — and set the set's `stage` to match. GW_SignoffRecorded after this reads the record back, so this step cannot be skipped by completing it: a sign-off that left no attestation loops here again."
msgstr ""

#: processes/global-tasks.bpmn:82
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "What the work is and why, what is already measured with its provenance, how it will be done, and what would falsify the approach. The work item is already taken up when the process starts, so a sibling session sees the work before the brief is written."
msgstr ""

#: processes/global-tasks.bpmn:28
#. Diagram label
msgid "Work plan (beans)"
msgstr ""

#: processes/global-tasks.bpmn:88
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Work the PRs `seed:ready` named until the source settles: land or close the heavy movers and the next layer's PRs, bring the layer's open PRs to five or fewer, and finish any move in flight. Fix a red rehearsal or a discovery miss where it is. Nothing is seeded from here; it goes back to the gateway, which re-asks."
msgstr ""

